WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.320
On a clear night, pick out two stars that
look exactly as bright as each other.

2
00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:09.560
To your eye, they're twins:
two equal points of light.

3
00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:11.890
Yet stars differ hugely.

4
00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:15.640
One star can give out 40
times the Sun's power.

5
00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:19.990
So if two stars look the same, how can
we tell which one really gives out more

6
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.090
light?

7
00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:26.060
In this mission, you'll meet luminosity:
the total power a star emits,

8
00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:27.630
measured in watts.

9
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:32.400
Then you'll link a star's power to
its surface temperature and its size.

10
00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:37.410
Your mission: find out how we can tell
which star really gives out more light.
